{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The daughter of a Canaanite man.</b> As its Targum renders it: a merchant (תגרא) — not an actual Canaanite. For Judah walked in the way of his fathers, and Heaven forbid that he should marry from the daughters of the Canaanite. Their wives were Egyptian, Ammonite, Moabite, and of the lineage of Yishmael and the sons of Keturah. And because of this, Scripture specified regarding Shaul son of Shimon (Genesis 46:10): ״ושאול בן הכנענית״ — to teach you that she alone among them was such. And even concerning her, our Rabbis, of blessed memory, held that she was not literally a Canaanite, and they said: this is Dinah, who was violated by a Canaanite."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:31.459279011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}